# Run r1102b slice 5, group A boot 1 (superflat, prep_srv.sh OUT s5a A ...; setup and toml edits: s5_setup.md).
# Rows: SQ-CDJ5 fix rerun (SQ-CDJ-12, SQ-MDP-18, SQ-VTD8-02 b/c), Jar fluid pipes, SQ-RB2, SQ-DRK, SQ-FCB, SQ-PST, SQ-PSD-01..05,
# SQ-PSM-01, SQ-PSF, SQ-PSU. Pre-boot toml: [pickling_jar] stallWhenFull = false (old Vintage file, carried into the CD
# file at boot), CD [stem_fruit] second/third/fourthFruitMinutes = 0 and maxFruits = 3 (one side stays empty: SQ-PSF-05/06).
# Home: marker tagged s5home at the console position (world spawn), capture S5H (y = S5H2 = the air layer above the
# superflat grass). Work sites, offsets from S5H: small rows z +20..+56, x +18..+70; PST pads x +40..+77, z +60..+97;
# far forceloaded site x +400 (JFP, FCB-07: chunk unload/reload away from spawn chunks and bots); PSU-04 bots x -200 / +200.
# Order: boot-log rows, probes, block rows, long rows (PSF-08 wait, PST pads, PSU-04 night), then FCB-07 (/reload) last.
# Every kjsexpect / kjsreject row is before FCB-07's /reload. No row here needs /cegen (item physics and WTHIT silk-touch
# generators write client data / reports only).
# Bots (perfBot, survival, invulnerable): one name per row. "break" = /s5 break (ServerPlayerGameMode.destroyBlock).
pace 2

## S5A-00 | setup: home marker, clock, weather, far site forceload (not a queue row)
bootexpect Done \(
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["s5home"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home,limit=1] Pos
